WEBVTT

00:00:00.161 --> 00:00:06.040
NIST SP 800-82 Revision 3 provides practical guidance for operational technology security.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.760
It broadens the discussion beyond traditional industrial control systems while keeping

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:10.620
physical process,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:15.030
safety, reliability, and availability at the center of security decisions.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:18.820
Effective programs understand their assets, topology, communication, dependencies,

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:21.630
threats, vulnerabilities, and operational consequences.

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:25.845
Risk management connects that evidence to accountable decisions about architecture,

00:00:25.845 --> 00:00:28.697
controls, remediation, residual risk, and recovery.

00:00:28.697 --> 00:00:32.680
Defense in depth combines physical protection, segmentation, access control,

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:36.915
secure remote access, monitoring, vulnerability management, backups,

00:00:36.915 --> 00:00:38.525
and incident response.

00:00:38.525 --> 00:00:41.425
Architecture should prevent unnecessary direct access and provide controlled,

00:00:41.425 --> 00:00:45.045
observable paths between enterprise and operational functions.

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:46.665
Security must also be maintained.

00:00:46.665 --> 00:00:51.090
Inventory, configuration baselines, change control, patch planning, logging, training,

00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:51.480
exercises,

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:56.033
and lifecycle management keep controls effective as technology and operations evolve.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:01:00.035
Evidence should demonstrate that controls work without creating unacceptable process risk.

00:01:00.035 --> 00:01:03.680
The publication guides decisions but does not replace site-specific judgment.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:07.620
Cybersecurity professionals, engineers, operators, safety teams, vendors,

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.440
and leadership must collaborate.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:11.520
The strongest outcome is not a completed checklist;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:14.735
it is a resilient operation that can prevent, detect, respond to,

00:01:14.735 --> 00:01:18.760
and recover from cyber events while continuing to protect people, mission, equipment,

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.040
and the physical process.
